    endPoint: "Dehradun",
    description: "The Hampta Pass Trek is one of the most visually diverse treks in the Indian Himalayas. Located in Himachal Pradesh, this trek is famous for its unique crossover from the lush green valleys of Kullu to the stark, barren landscapes of Spiti. This striking contrast in terrain makes Hampta Pass a favorite among trekkers who want to experience two completely different Himalayan ecosystems in a single journey. Starting from Manali, the trek begins in dense pine forests, river streams, and alpine meadows. As you move forward, the landscape gradually transforms into wide-open valleys surrounded by towering peaks. The trail passes through scenic campsites like Chika and Balu Ka Ghera, each offering breathtaking views and serene surroundings. The highlight of the trek is crossing Hampta Pass at an altitude of approximately 14,100 ft. The climb to the pass is challenging yet rewarding, involving snow crossings, steep ascents, and panoramic views of the surrounding mountains. Standing at the pass, you can witness the transition from green valleys to the cold desert of Spiti, a sight that is truly unforgettable. Another major highlight is the visit to Chandratal Lake, a high-altitude glacial lake known for its crystal-clear blue waters. Surrounded by barren mountains, the lake creates a surreal contrast against the rugged terrain of Spiti. What makes the Hampta Pass Trek unique is its accessibility and adventure balance. It offers just the right amount of challenge for trekkers who want to push their limits without extreme technical difficulty. The trek is ideal for both beginners with good fitness levels and experienced trekkers looking for a short yet rewarding expedition. From river crossings and glacier walks to dramatic landscapes and high-altitude passes, the Hampta Pass Trek delivers a complete Himalayan experience packed into five days. It is a journey that combines adventure, natural beauty, and the thrill of crossing from one valley to another.",
